\intbl\row}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 HOW TO SET IT OPTIMALLY (for the less experienced - so you don't overdo it):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Safe quasi-CVBR ~128k stereo: {\f1 -b 128000 --peak-bitrate 160000 --vbr-reservoir 6000}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Do NOT set {\f1 --max-bits-frame} BELOW the average or {\f1 --min-bits-frame} ABOVE the average - that fights the target and ruins quality.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\f1 --vbr-reservoir} is auto-clamped to the ceiling, so it's safe to experiment.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Measured for real (4s variable signal, 128k stereo): CBR default spread 95-167 kbps; with {\f1 --vbr-reservoir 8000 --peak-bitrate 192000} spread 36-158 kbps (breathes harder, average held); {\f1 --bitres-mode 2} spread 127.8-128.2 (rigid). All fully decodable.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Limitation: this is a CBR+reservoir engine, not true ABR like LAME. Swings are moderate (6144 bits/channel limit), but this is that "light flight" of AAC.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 10. Audiophile / extreme (opt-in, beyond the typical range)\par}
