\intbl\row}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 BANDWIDTH ABOVE 20 kHz (audiophile): FDK has a hardcoded cap {\f1 min(20000, sr/2)} on the core bandwidth \u8212- even with a 96 kHz input and high bitrate, nothing above 20 kHz is actually coded (your suspicion was correct). {\f1 --uncap-bandwidth} lifts this cap; then {\f1 --core-cutoff} controls the bandwidth all the way up to sr/2.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Measured (96 kHz input, LC 400k, broadband noise):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab without uncap, {\f1 --core-cutoff 40000}: verbose 20000 Hz, energy >20 kHz ~= 0%.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\f1 --core-cutoff 40000 --uncap-bandwidth}: verbose 40000 Hz, energy 20-24 kHz ~10%, 24-32 kHz ~20%, 32-44 kHz ~20% \u8212- full band up to 40 kHz actually coded.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Audiophile preset (full bandwidth + manual masking, for 190+ kbps):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 fdkaac-franken-x64.exe -p 2 -b 320000 --uncap-bandwidth --core-cutoff 40000 \\\line
    --ath-scale 200 -o out.m4a in96k.wav\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --ath-scale <256} lowers the masking thresholds (cleaner, more bits for detail) \u8212- sensible when you have a large bitrate margin. Note: bandwidth >20 kHz and extreme settings may be rejected by some decoders (outside the typical spec) \u8212- a conscious opt-in.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 11. MP4/M4A container \u8212- which boxes are necessary, and what can be cut\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 An .m4a file is a set of nested "boxes" (atoms). Verified what is what:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MANDATORY (without them the file is UNPLAYABLE \u8212- there are no switches for them): {\f1 ftyp}, {\f1 mdat} (raw audio data), and the skeleton {\f1 moov} \u8594 ? {\f1 mvhd} + {\f1 trak} \u8594 ? {\f1 tkhd} \u8594 ? {\f1 mdia} ({\f1 mdhd}/{\f1 hdlr}/{\f1 minf} \u8594 ? {\f1 smhd}/{\f1 dinf}/{\f1 stbl} with the tables {\f1 stsd}/{\f1 stts}/{\f1 stsc}/{\f1 stsz}/{\f1 stco}). This is the minimal file map required by the ISO standard \u8212- every decoder needs it to even find and play the sound. Cutting them makes no sense (result: a corrupt file).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 OPTIONAL (can be disabled) \u8212- the entire block {\f1 udta} \u8594 ? {\f1 meta} \u8594 ? {\f1 ilst}, i.e.:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab the encoder identification tag ({\f1 \u169 ?too}, now "PompAAC based on \u8230 ?"),\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\f1 iTunSMPB} \u8212- encoder delay data for seamless (gapless) playback,\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab all tags (title, artist, album, etc.).\sa180\par}
{
